# Electrum data .gitignore

# macOS artifacts
._*
.DS_Store

# Windows artifacts
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
*.tmp

# Electrum runtime artifacts
/blockchain_headers
/cache/
/certs/
/daemon
/daemon_rpc_socket
/forks/
/plugins/
/recent_servers
/config
/wallets/
/testnet/
/testnet4/
/regtest/

# Launcher artifacts
# The launchers under macos/scripts/electrum/ and linux/scripts/electrum/
# each bind a unix socket here, and release it, to learn whether the
# filesystem can hold the one Electrum's daemon needs. Each removes it on
# every branch of that test, so it is left behind only where the launcher
# dies between the bind and the removal. The suffix is the launcher's
# process id.
#
# Two names, because the platforms have not converged yet. macOS's is kept
# shorter than daemon_rpc_socket so the test is never the more fragile of
# the two: perl truncates an over-long socket path rather than refusing it,
# which binds at a name the removal does not match and refuses every later
# run. Linux's python raises instead, so it never leaves that residue and
# still carries the longer name. Both patterns stay until it does converge.
/.probe.*
/.portanode-socket-probe.*
